Experiment: Working with Sniffers for Monitoring Network Communication Using Wireshark in Kali Linux
Step-by-Step Procedure
Step 1: Open Terminal
1.	Log in to Kali Linux.
2.	Open the terminal.
 
Step 2: Launch Wireshark
Type the following command:
Sudo wireshark
Or open it from:
Applications → Sniffing & Spoofing → Wireshark
  
Step 3: Select a Network Interface
1.	Wireshark displays available interfaces.
2.	Select the active interface:
o	eth0 (Ethernet)
o	wlan0 (Wireless)
3.	Double-click the interface to start packet capturing.

Step 4: Start Capturing Packets
1.	Click the blue Shark Fin icon.
2.	Network packets begin appearing in real time.

Step 5: Generate Network Traffic
Open a browser and visit websites such as:
https://www.google.com
https://www.wikipedia.org
Or execute:
ping google.com
This generates packets for analysis.
  
Step 6: Stop Packet Capture
1.	Click the red Stop button.
2.	Packet capture is halted.

Step 7: Analyze Captured Packets
Observe the three Wireshark panes:
Packet List Pane
Displays captured packets.
Packet Details Pane
Shows protocol information.
Packet Bytes Pane
Displays packet contents in hexadecimal format.
 
Step 8: Apply Display Filters
View HTTP Traffic-http
View DNS Traffic-dns
View TCP Packets-tcp
View ICMP (Ping) Packets-icmp
View Traffic from Specific IP-ip.addr == 8.8.8.8
Press Enter after entering the filter.
 
Step 9: Inspect Packet Details
1.	Select a packet.
2.	Expand:
o	Ethernet II
o	Internet Protocol (IP)
o	Transmission Control Protocol (TCP)
o	Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP)
3.	Note:
o	Source IP Address
o	Destination IP Address
o	Protocol Used
o	Packet Length

Step 10: Follow a TCP Stream
1.	Right-click a TCP packet.
2.	Select:
Follow → TCP Stream
3.	View communication between client and server.
4.	Close the window after analysis.
 
Step 11: Save the Capture
1.	Click File → Save As.
2.	Save as:
network_capture.pcapng
3.	Choose a destination folder.

Step 12: Reopen Saved Capture
1.	Select:
File → Open
2.	Browse to the saved. pcapng file.
3.	Open it for further analysis.
